Nexix manuals

The original V7 manual files in sections 0 through 8 are preserved unchanged.
They document historical V7. Availability of a page does not mean the command
or every interface is implemented in Nexix 0.1.0 yet.

Nexix uses native x86_64 ELF programs and native device/interface adaptations,
not PDP-11 executable layouts or hardware. The historical header excerpts in
/usr/man/include are for documentation only; installed development headers
are under /usr/include. Files retain V7 access/modification/change timestamps,
with the system epoch initialized from RTC. There is no file birth timestamp.

Use man 7 nexix for native manual-reading instructions and adaptations.
